oe Oakhart","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":3,"unsigned":13},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"c2c23137498be047c1726cf1ebf25ec0355ce40f14f31dd3a200b291ffdc689e","event_uuid":"3f5e98ee-63b3-40bb-80ce-e804ab8bbf2d","position":{"commit_sha":"fda845728257ad68ef9e4390410f520fda245d79","position":"1784231773140872186-3f5e98ee-63b3-40bb-80ce-e804ab8bbf2d"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"07449f6c82751ec1e175ff1280f2477bb7e92e46f72befbae33a557d75158955","event_uuid":"c944443a-40e6-46bb-b08c-61451a7723c8","position":{"commit_sha":"a237fe14cb7ec3bf57b83d5ad2ba2173f681c135","position":"1785330330042640429-c944443a-40e6-46bb-b08c-61451a7723c8"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"a8cd0b7104daf5a295ae6ee0f6af00d87694eaf7fc0b01ebd9e727cc5a28c5d1","event_uuid":"7ef08fec-0d34-4b02-ae18-15fb6656f253","position":{"commit_sha":"39d02835bfc8a904d057691768d01aaed46e2ac3","position":"1785330782237190292-7ef08fec-0d34-4b02-ae18-15fb6656f253"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-209_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"90514dff-8b46-4f42-ae53-a1e35fc50ef6","comments":[{"author":"Joe Oakhart","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"FORCE_CLAIM: plan-review gate bypassed by user approval — no plan-review attestation was verified. Reason: \"re-certify under current signing scheme (opcert HMAC->Ed25519 migration)\".","timestamp":1784088660602600001},{"author":"Joe Oakhart","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Re-certification under the current Ed25519 signing scheme (the parallel opcert epic migrated the completion-signing scheme after this ticket's original close; original attestation now reads unknown_scheme). CI/make-pass evidence: this ticket's change is MERGED to main carrying Verified=+1 (clean-env CI: build/test/lint/typecheck) AND LLM-Review=+1; local make lint/typecheck green; all acceptance-criteria tests present and passing.","timestamp":1784088666924827001}],"created_at":1784067232188658001,"creation_channel":"unknown","deps":[],"description":"## Why\n\nThe plan-review `REVIEW_RESULT` sidecar is the only durable record of a review's four passes, but\nits `_slim` step drops the pass-1 `evidence` and `scenarios` fields, and it does not persist the\nnumeric `block_threshold`/`blocking_enabled` each finding was judged against (these are resolved\nfrom the criteria registry at decision time and then discarded). Without them an auditor cannot see\na finding's grounding quotes or the exact decision boundary that was applied.\n\n## What\n\nExtend the plan-review sidecar to a new schema version `plan_review_result_v2` that additionally\npersists, per finding: the pass-1 `evidence[]` and `scenarios[]`, and the resolved `block_threshold`\n(float) and `blocking_enabled` (bool) that pass-3 used. All existing fields and the all-buckets\npooling (blocking + advisory + overflow + indeterminate + dropped) are unchanged.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/sidecar.py` — bump `SCHEMA` to `plan_review_result_v2`; stop stripping\n  `evidence`/`scenarios` in `_slim`; thread the resolved `block_threshold`/`blocking_enabled` from\n  the pass-3 decision into each persisted finding; `latest_review_result` accepts both `v1` and `v2`.\n- `src/rebar/llm/review_kernel/decide.py` — expose the resolved `block_threshold`/`blocking_enabled`\n  on each finding's decision output (the `ThresholdResolver` result is currently used then dropped).\n\n## Approach rationale\n\nBump the schema and widen the payload rather than write a parallel record, so the single existing\nemit/prune/read path carries the richer data unchanged in shape. The resolved threshold is captured\nat the exact point pass-3 applies it, which is the only place it is knowable without re-reading the\nregistry (avoiding historical drift).\n\n## Compatibility & rollback\n\n`v1` sidecars remain valid and are read with the new fields absent (readers treat missing\nthreshold/evidence as \"not recorded\"). No backfill. Reverting restores the `v1` payload; already-\nwritten `v2` events remain readable by the tolerant reader. Adding fields to the payload does not\nchange the reducer-ignored status or the event type, so older clients keep skipping the event.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Running `review-plan` emits a `REVIEW_RESULT` event whose `schema` is `plan_review_result_v2`\n      and whose every persisted finding carries `evidence`, `scenarios`, `block_threshold`, and\n      `blocking_enabled`. Oracle: an in-process integration test drives a review with a stub LLM\n      runner and asserts on the emitted event JSON via the real sidecar emit path (test-design §3\n      producer/consumer shape).\n- [ ] `pass3_decide`/`pass3_over_findings` expose the resolved `block_threshold`/`blocking_enabled`\n      on each finding. Oracle: a unit test against the real decide functions asserting the fields\n      are present with the resolved values.\n- [ ] `latest_review_result` reads both a `v1` and a `v2` sidecar file without error, reporting the\n      new fields absent for `v1`. Oracle: a unit test feeding one hand-written `v1` and one `v2`\n      event.\n- [ ] `make lint && make typecheck && make test` pass.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/sidecar.py","reason":"enrich payload to v2 + tolerant reader"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/review_kernel/decide.py","reason":"expose resolved threshold on decision"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_reopened_at":1784088657387074001,"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["parent","ba33-2310-f6c6-4bd6"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"ba33-2310-f6c6-4bd6","parent_status_uuid":"01c51c54-39b9-4dbc-9759-df03f69c3f29","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"4e19-5846-0e3f-4882","ticket_type":"story","title":"plan-review sidecar -> lossless v2 (evidence, scenarios, thresholds)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["9a6658f2-5614-4a4f-9831-57834946304d","0b96d738-b6b5-4f67-93cf-f106ec79126f","dc5c7479-6ca0-42c9-afb9-0c008b2c5455","321e5155-bad3-48a2-a8df-d30c875e439b","0a8cf1fa-62ef-4da0-8085-6d255fefb1ff","e51621b6-8f44-420b-ac58-97e055673107","bfc78599-30a4-4b5f-be7c-12a2eb1b8bf7","6c5b0f42-e10c-487e-acfe-c14ac3aa7e65","2c56cd97-293d-4cc0-ae6b-5914686eff03","d26a1dea-5bb5-4726-a953-9c499dd95598","4503faea-512e-4fc7-ac8a-a05ce467e904","68245e85-0cd7-494b-8fa7-21a6ac635a4b","251cef42-fb1f-413b-a304-f35794811f4c","1d083cd7-bae8-4c18-b0c3-6fcf267a566d","01c51c54-39b9-4dbc-9759-df03f69c3f29","a361e489-9516-40f8-875b-03ce00b3265b","468e2b89-84ef-4d4b-b22b-2fc7f622eafe","3e086c88-03b7-4339-8116-db1117b0ade5","3f5e98ee-63b3-40bb-80ce-e804ab8bbf2d","c944443a-40e6-46bb-b08c-61451a7723c8","7ef08fec-0d34-4b02-ae18-15fb6656f253","d2b58273-b00e-45fe-877f-95de3d8a52e1","8d33c175-c1d5-4ab0-80ec-7fe3d0c6f0ae","9c3452f2-c049-